## Why IP Quality Matters

Platforms like TikTok, Instagram, Facebook, Amazon, and streaming services are now much better at identifying IP types.

A regular datacenter IP is easy to detect. If an IP has been abused, shared by too many users, or listed in risk databases, accounts using it may face problems such as:

- Registration failure
- Login verification
- Traffic throttling
- Shadow bans
- Payment risk checks
- Account suspension
- Streaming region restrictions

A **residential IP** is different.

Residential IPs are assigned by internet service providers to real household broadband users. To most platforms, they look closer to normal local users.

LisaHost also offers **dual-ISP residential IPs**. These IPs are usually associated with two internet service providers and generally have lower risk scores. In some independent tests, certain LisaHost IP ranges showed very low fraud scores on IP reputation checking tools.

This is why dual-ISP residential IPs are usually more expensive than ordinary native IP VPS products.

LisaHost’s product line is built around this exact demand:

- Ordinary native IP VPS
- Dual-ISP residential IP VPS
- Regional native IP VPS
- Real residential VDS products

Each product targets a different type of user.

